<title>UK: Sema off on Merrill caution, stock overhang.</title>
<headline>Sema off on Merrill caution, stock overhang.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sema Group Plc fell on Monday as analysts at Merrill Lynch took the stock off their &quot;bull list&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shares in the Anglo-French technology group were down 35p at 10.95 stg by 1522 GMT. Dealers said an overhang of stock had also weighed on the shares.  </p>
<p>Philip Wolstencroft, UK strategist at Merrill Lynch, said FirstBus Plc, Scottish Hydro-Electric Plc and Vaux Group Plc had been added to the bull list.</p>
<p>FirstBus shares climbed two pence to 223, Scottish Hydro gained four pence to 352-1/2 and Vaux rose 1/2p to 255-1/2.</p>
<p>BTP Plc was removed from the bull list along with Sema, while First Leisure and David S. Smith Plc were added to Merrill's &quot;bear list&quot;, Wolstencroft said.</p>
<p>BTP shares were unchanged at 283-1/2p and First Leisure was also steady at 336-1/2p. David S. Smith shares fell 1-1/2p to 282-1/2.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
